      "claim": "The modern woman sculpture's folded drapery has its own distinct style that differs from the others.",
      "stance": "supports",
      "observation_ids": [ "img-k7-o0", "img-v9-o2" ],"grounds": "Observation img-k7-o0 describes the fabric as creating an impression of 'softness and fluidity' mimicking 'silk or fine linen,' with gentle curves. In contrast, observation img-v9-o2 (associated with another draped figure) states the surface is 'consistently smooth and continuous... reinforcing the impression of carved stone rather than draped cloth.' The contrast between the specific imitation of soft textile in img-k7-o0 and the solid stone impression in other descriptions supports the claim that this particular modern woman's folds have a unique stylistic effect."
